# Gate step — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq). Moved from an inline build.sh
# --check block by the .step series (2253-j2at batch 2): as a .step it is no
# build.sh edit, so it never makes intake HEAVY, and it runs in the pool (a
# read-only decider: it reads the tree and the diff, writes nothing).
#
# Order 702-eusw criterion 3: a build-number VERSION bump must never be swept
# into an unrelated commit. dd8fd63f bundled a VERSION bump into a security
# fix via `git add -A`; the mandated linux-next merge then imported a
# divergent VERSION the mandated pre-push gate refused, blocking the whole
# fleet. This guard refuses any NON-MERGE outgoing commit that changes VERSION
# alongside non-companion files (a merge inheriting VERSION is exempt — that
# is a legitimate catch-up, order 643-64bx). A clean release-bump commit
# (VERSION + Cargo files only) still passes.
STEP_DESC="Checking VERSION-bump isolation on outgoing commits (702-eusw)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/check-version-bump-isolation.lua"
STEP_ERROR="an outgoing commit sweeps a VERSION bump in with unrelated files — bump alone via a release/version-bump-* branch (702-eusw)"
STEP_OK="VERSION-bump isolation check passed"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="tlatoanis-macbook-air 2026-11-23 darwin ok:version-bump-isolation:no-comparable-range at 1af8ff01c (fleet-run)"
STEP_READS="scripts/lua/check-version-bump-isolation.lua"
